## 1. Deep Investigation of Existing Government & Commercial Platforms (15 Parameters)

We investigated 8 major Indian and international agricultural technology initiatives across government Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI), B2B SaaS, IoT precision farming, and mobile advisory apps.

### 1.1 Government of India Platforms

#### A. **FASAL** (Forecasting Agricultural output using Space, Agro-meteorology and Land-based observations)
* **Organization:** [Mahalanobis National Crop Forecast Centre (MNCFC)](https://www.ncfc.gov.in/fasal.html), Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare (MoA&FW), with technical support from ISRO.
* **Target Customers & Region:** Central and State Ministries across **20 states and 557 districts** in India ([Global Agriculture](https://www.global-agriculture.com/india-region/satellite-based-crop-monitoring-strengthens-indias-production-estimates/)).
* **Actual Capabilities & AI/ML:** Generates pre-harvest district-level acreage and production forecasts for **11 major crops** (rice, wheat, mustard, cotton, maize, soybean, groundnut, rabi pulses, sugarcane, jute, arhar) using optical and microwave satellite data combined with agro-meteorological and semi-physical crop yield models validated by Crop Cutting Experiments (CCEs) ([Lok Sabha Reply Annex, Mar 2026](https://sansad.in/getFile/loksabhaquestions/annex/187/AU1860_aH1Jxn.pdf?source=pqals)).
* **Plot-Level Support & Resource Optimization:** **No.** Operates at the **district level** for macro food-security planning. Does not provide farmer-facing irrigation or fertilizer timing recommendations.

#### B. **YES-TECH** (Yield Estimation System based on Technology)
* **Organization:** MoA&FW under [Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY)](https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2297646&reg=48&lang=1) and MNCFC.
* **Target Customers & Region:** State governments and crop insurance companies across India (rolled out from Kharif 2023 for paddy, wheat, and soybean) ([MNCFC Lok Sabha Reply](https://www.ncfc.gov.in/rti/parliamentquestions/LS%20question%20DY%20no.%201213%20reg.%20crop_losses1.pdf)).
* **Actual Capabilities & AI/ML:** Uses satellite remote sensing, UAV pilots, crop simulation models, and ML ensembles to estimate yields at the **Gram Panchayat (GP) level** to settle PMFBY insurance claims and reduce manual Crop Cutting Experiment disputes.
* **Limitations & Unexplored Gap:** Post-facto insurance settlement tool at the Gram Panchayat level; does not offer individual farmers mid-season counterfactual action recommendations to prevent yield loss or reduce water/urea waste.

#### C. **Krishi-DSS** (Krishi Decision Support System)
* **Organization:** [Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare and Department of Space (ISRO)](https://krishi-dss.gov.in/), launched August 2024 ([PIB Press Release](https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2045987)).
* **Target Customers & Region:** Policymakers, researchers, and agricultural officers nationwide.
* **Actual Capabilities & Data Sources:** Geospatial platform built on ISRO's **RISAT-1A** and **VEDAS** (Visualization of Earth observation Data and Archival System), integrating weather, groundwater levels, soil health, reservoir storage, and crop acreage mapping ([VisionIAS / PIB](https://visionias.in/current-affairs/news-today/2024-08-17/science-and-technology/satellite-based-agriculture-decision-support-system-launched)).
* **Limitations & Unexplored Gap:** Primarily a top-down geospatial visualization portal for institutional stakeholders; lacks a farmer-facing counterfactual optimization engine that translates pixel-level `SAVI/NDMI` trajectories into rupee-quantified irrigation/urea delay decisions.

#### D. **AgriStack & Digital Crop Survey (UFSI)**
* **Organization:** [Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare](https://agristack.gov.in/), approved September 2024 with a ₹2,817 crore outlay ([Creuto UFSI Analysis, Sep 2026](https://creuto.com/agristack-api-ufsi-farmer-registry-agritech)).
* **Actual Capabilities:** Digital Public Infrastructure comprising three federated registries: **Farmer Registry** (11 crore Farmer IDs target by 2026–27), **Geo-Referenced Village Maps**, and **Crop Sown Registry** via state portals like [AgriStack Telangana Digital Crop Survey](https://tgdcs.agristack.gov.in/crop-survey-tg/). Exposes the **Unified Farmer Service Interface (UFSI)** API gateway for consent-based verification.
* **Opportunity for Our Project:** AgriStack is an **infrastructure rail (like UPI)**, not an AI yield/resource optimizer. Building our solution to ingest AgriStack plot polygons and crop-sown records aligns directly with India's 2026 DPI architecture.

