### 1.2 Commercial Startups & International Platforms

#### E. **Cropin** (Cropin Cloud — SmartFarm / SmartRisk / Akshara)
* **Organization:** [Cropin Technology Solutions](https://www.cropin.com/) (Bengaluru, India; global operations in 90+ countries).
* **Target Customers:** Enterprise agribusinesses, seed companies, food processors, banks, and government agencies (B2B / B2G).
* **Capabilities & AI/ML:** Combines Sentinel/Landsat satellite imagery, field-officer logs, and weather data to forecast regional crop supply, monitor contract farms, and assess climate risk ([Cropin Blog, Feb 2026](https://www.cropin.com/blogs/satellite-vs-ground-intelligence-enterprise-farm-scale/)).
* **Pricing & Limitations:** Enterprise SaaS licensing costing lakhs/crores per enterprise contract. Inaccessible to an individual 2-acre smallholder farmer without corporate sponsorship.

#### F. **Fasal** (Wolkus Technology Solutions)
* **Organization:** [Fasal](https://www.fasal.co/) (Bengaluru, India; Series A funded with $19.4M total funding per [Tracxn Oct 2026](https://tracxn.com/d/companies/fasal/__oNAHl8UEovECojkNpiJPyCUx9OCZTmEr14g5hIUusIU)).
* **Target Customers:** Medium-to-large commercial horticulture farmers (grapes, pomegranates, apples, chilli, tomato).
* **Capabilities & Tech Stack:** Deploys on-farm IoT hardware (`Fasal Sense`, `FasalJet`, `FasalJet Pro`) with soil moisture/temperature probes and micro-weather stations pushing telemetry via MQTT/HTTP to AWS SageMaker ML models for precision irrigation and pest alerts ([Meteor Case Study](https://blog.meteor.com/how-fasal-helps-farmers-grow-smarter-with-meteor-3f1891707a4)).
* **Pricing & Limitations:** **Hardware-dependent.** Requires purchasing physical IoT sensor nodes and paying recurring subscription fees—economically viable for high-value horticulture orchards, but unviable for 120 million cereal/pulse smallholder plots.

#### G. **DeHaat**
* **Organization:** Green Agrevolution Pvt. Ltd. (Patna/Gurugram, India).
* **Target Customers:** Smallholder farmers across Bihar, UP, Jharkhand, Odisha, Maharashtra, and Rajasthan.
* **Capabilities:** Full-stack marketplace offering seed/fertilizer inputs, general Hindi/regional advisory, market linkage, and basic satellite/IoT pilots ([Mayank Digital Labs](https://www.mayankdigitallabs.in/blog/ai-crop-disease-detection-farmers-2026)).
* **Limitations:** Primarily an input-commerce and human call-center/franchisee network (`DeHaat Centers`); advisory is largely rule-based agronomy rather than plot-level counterfactual satellite-soil-weather simulation.

#### H. **Plantix** (PEAT GmbH)
* **Organization:** PEAT GmbH (Berlin, Germany; >50 million downloads globally, with India as its largest user base per [Mayank Digital Labs, Aug 2026](https://www.mayankdigitallabs.in/blog/ai-crop-disease-detection-farmers-2026)).
* **Target Customers:** Smallholder farmers with Android smartphones.
* **Capabilities & AI/ML:** Deep Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) trained to diagnose 400+ crop diseases and pest damages from close-up leaf photographs in 4 seconds (e.g., 91% accuracy on rice blast, 89% on wheat leaf rust).
* **Limitations:** **Purely reactive visual pathology.** Does not predict end-of-season crop yield, does not integrate Sentinel-1/2 satellite moisture/vegetation trajectories, and does not optimize irrigation volume or urea leaching windows.

